Subject: [LOCAL] simple: allow the Poco app to avoid its broken binned mode

On the current beryllium kernel, IMX363 1920x1080 captures contain a
four-column colour pattern rather than the advertised two-column Bayer
pattern. Full-resolution raw captures have the correct Bayer layout.
Opt in only from this app, until the kernel's binned sensor mode is fixed.
SoftISP still scales the full sensor input to the requested preview size.

--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -693,6 +693,17 @@
  */
 void SimpleCameraData::tryPipeline(unsigned int code, const Size &size)
 {
+	/*
+	 * Local beryllium workaround, deliberately opt-in. Do not reinterpret
+	 * the corrupt binned output as a different CFA or calibrate against it.
+	 */
+	const char *fullSensor = utils::secure_getenv("SPECTRE_IMX363_FULL_SENSOR");
+	if (fullSensor && std::string(fullSensor) == "1" &&
+	    sensor_->model() == "imx363" && size == Size(1920, 1080)) {
+		LOG(SimplePipeline, Info)
+			<< "Skipping unverified IMX363 binned mode; using full sensor";
+		return;
+	}
